#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172039 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171845 :question/id #uuid "0444de80-19f1-5251-b159-5dc55756bb19" :question/math-academy-id "e-8506" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = -2xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n\n- At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y) = -2xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} = f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y) = 0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\left.\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} \\right|_{(x,y)} =f(x,y)  \\gt     0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x, y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\left.\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} \\right|_{(x,y)} = f(x,y)  \\lt     0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x, y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\left.\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} \\right|_{(x,y)} = f(x,y)  \\gt     0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x, y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048480 :topic/difficulty 1.0 :topic/id #uuid "a300d19e-159b-5193-a238-66665089cb1c" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129218} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129219}] :topic/math-academy-id 2076 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048795}] :topic/title "Solving Two-Variable Nonlinear Inequalities"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172645 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "817b7d0e-081e-5f65-8394-7b2aa4d4b020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438622} {:answer/id #uuid "51e53bdb-ad9b-5fde-96ad-6776ae72ee75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51e53bdb-ad9b-5fde-96ad-6776ae72ee75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438623} :answer-field/id #uuid "87784eaa-7f37-5cfd-bf94-f676298d7eb1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "434b294c-ea0b-5331-849a-fa7706de7c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438624} {:answer/id #uuid "a7afa29d-56b9-57cf-9491-c30536a33167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "434b294c-ea0b-5331-849a-fa7706de7c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438624} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8a8760c-7b07-5de6-8cb4-15b2d479532a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005ad32f-fad3-5e4b-9876-1dea386fda92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438626} {:answer/id #uuid "da8dc176-0ecf-5a7b-9dd5-659d6a397554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da8dc176-0ecf-5a7b-9dd5-659d6a397554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438627} :answer-field/id #uuid "83dc6e63-ac75-598d-8eb8-29e5e8e60f37" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439342}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd7005de-da4a-5aae-a0ea-f0c01c178438" :question/math-academy-id "q-96767" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=2xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172648 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3c0e91a-8719-5dbf-92fb-86a7721ef654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440023} {:answer/id #uuid "55bf2da5-d708-5480-8ab8-1441064688e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3c0e91a-8719-5dbf-92fb-86a7721ef654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440023} :answer-field/id #uuid "402941ab-b608-5343-ad5f-8ac1f83f99c2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e82d40ad-c41b-57a8-a872-ff25ef67196e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440025} {:answer/id #uuid "fa689d24-4924-55c6-8219-2928fe0f7962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa689d24-4924-55c6-8219-2928fe0f7962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440026} :answer-field/id #uuid "097f13ad-dd16-5c08-84cd-9bb354ae065e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440370} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "934c3087-576f-525a-b55f-b5b5ad9f17fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440027} {:answer/id #uuid "926d422e-445c-57ec-9858-ba3785eafd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "926d422e-445c-57ec-9858-ba3785eafd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440028} :answer-field/id #uuid "f873dbf2-94f8-5412-b40f-fa9306104dc1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440371}] :question/id #uuid "1142a38e-b72d-5615-beec-20a68972aab2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97483" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = xy^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "For xy^2, y^2 is positive in every open quadrant, so the slope has the sign of x. It is negative in quadrants II and III, and positive in quadrant I."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253595 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9de7b235-2d26-5638-9c0e-50fbf024a420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437558} {:answer/id #uuid "a52d85f3-9510-5691-8cd4-aec1cbec2217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a52d85f3-9510-5691-8cd4-aec1cbec2217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437559} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3564637-e4ca-5adf-93e8-018d20d50745" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c57c046d-8a73-5f59-9a49-b2aed7a95848" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437560} {:answer/id #uuid "70926e08-7c1e-54d5-abf7-3b2825ba6a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70926e08-7c1e-54d5-abf7-3b2825ba6a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437561} :answer-field/id #uuid "569f6144-ac61-57e2-9faa-b2202fc52224" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438809} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81024236-c12a-5269-b2cd-e687e5de0a78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437562} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9cd6b7-f2cf-568e-a96b-b42a586b87cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d9cd6b7-f2cf-568e-a96b-b42a586b87cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437563} :answer-field/id #uuid "e68102cc-579c-585f-8f10-9a83a65a0a06" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438810}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d92f1990-38b8-544d-a68e-c6daa48b1c4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119766" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=6xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253597 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf9f9a0-fe1d-58a6-a9a8-b5a5e2a9514b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437564} {:answer/id #uuid "c6011e7b-933f-5512-8d31-3053e17fd0dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caf9f9a0-fe1d-58a6-a9a8-b5a5e2a9514b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437564} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecff95c2-727a-5dae-ab02-1414391132f2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "791f7229-c5a9-5faf-8875-969a85713e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437566} {:answer/id #uuid "a8d04d15-d334-5842-ab9f-31f5f6d0fe8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "791f7229-c5a9-5faf-8875-969a85713e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437566} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fdf80c4-0c0f-5731-bd95-650894071c56" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f793cf-e920-5057-905e-6cd6b37d67be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437568} {:answer/id #uuid "42e66d50-d188-5d08-9d22-fe5a8a4b8fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42e66d50-d188-5d08-9d22-fe5a8a4b8fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437569} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3f69ac8-557d-5583-a34f-bae77d1add4a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438813}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e15411d6-1039-50b8-8bc5-cef852747aab" :question/math-academy-id "q-119769" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-5xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-5xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2acc8d45-b3cb-5472-808a-0ded96068ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437570} {:answer/id #uuid "5634aa7f-d685-513c-b71c-dd484269de1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2acc8d45-b3cb-5472-808a-0ded96068ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437570} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a1d4246-8605-5a10-a963-fb61cf7903ea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438814} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc34f3d5-600f-5ec4-ada6-979b186201d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437572} {:answer/id #uuid "a49a1c0b-79f3-538f-b749-b1d3bd1e40e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a49a1c0b-79f3-538f-b749-b1d3bd1e40e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437573} :answer-field/id #uuid "c41e5771-7f8b-5c44-9d14-38d54c1a1ee9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438815} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59bd4a0c-4bd0-55c9-ad16-d8c9e25d7727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437574} {:answer/id #uuid "a8d6c719-9178-53d2-a8bc-b7c6358a8cc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59bd4a0c-4bd0-55c9-ad16-d8c9e25d7727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437574} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a4fd295-2359-5c48-b9f5-fdc795da9a6a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438816}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c47e99b0-49b1-5362-97e1-164913960980" :question/math-academy-id "q-119774" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/d1/d1e4f48450a7f2032d755a5255d1a1e8a726dd16d273dae5dc1e587826d5ce58.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95bf5c87-5d3a-5cc2-9253-891ef7730177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438628} {:answer/id #uuid "3d5d5215-469a-5799-ba24-eb8bc4c358d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95bf5c87-5d3a-5cc2-9253-891ef7730177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438628} :answer-field/id #uuid "f545d324-f9c3-507e-983b-fd1001340ff1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b8f3b3-189f-5b75-9ccc-ddd834e75d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438630} {:answer/id #uuid "d83106e2-c95a-541f-8d33-b2ba054c50ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83106e2-c95a-541f-8d33-b2ba054c50ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438631} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7dbe69a-f051-5886-8cde-e2c1753c8657" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439344} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25dae65-1d55-511a-b24e-a8cb350771d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438632} {:answer/id #uuid "41b3f2e3-0dfd-5365-982e-fd4103306c05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e25dae65-1d55-511a-b24e-a8cb350771d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438632} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8887387-6555-5bd2-8c67-a09c271d9b0f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439345}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ebbc31b-8f74-56d3-8d4f-392a8aeeda85" :question/math-academy-id "q-97477" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af5c066d-bd1b-5916-a240-8a09350060cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438634} {:answer/id #uuid "e033cbd9-4a9c-558a-b84e-515ba29c5965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af5c066d-bd1b-5916-a240-8a09350060cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438634} :answer-field/id #uuid "86f3af7d-b3a9-5b53-9913-e3d5d3053834" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439346} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adc85b15-3131-50c7-b7d4-2e649a9fb136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438636} {:answer/id #uuid "409eb813-3391-5d94-b0e1-4012a919fc2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "409eb813-3391-5d94-b0e1-4012a919fc2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438637} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdc4db1c-cf09-591b-bae6-192098ed008b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439347} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e92256da-0966-5c42-98d2-bb15e2c0f12d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438638} {:answer/id #uuid "eea8981c-85f6-57b9-bcd6-78db1679f73c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e92256da-0966-5c42-98d2-bb15e2c0f12d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438638} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdfcbe44-29db-570c-9bd7-2b09381a9273" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439348}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ffe3a0e-6b8b-5f1d-8f45-5dd040381266" :question/math-academy-id "q-97482" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=9xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=9xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360823 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02991364-b415-5593-9a79-441d1bc3e524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438640} {:answer/id #uuid "8149ff14-001b-5709-8795-c16ffb823815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8149ff14-001b-5709-8795-c16ffb823815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438641} :answer-field/id #uuid "67616cec-be6c-5e26-881c-d38eeb8cbc05" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27aca29d-adac-5da5-979e-bf019c9f7e9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438642} {:answer/id #uuid "72677ee7-465d-51d2-8a9e-8bf69e29a86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72677ee7-465d-51d2-8a9e-8bf69e29a86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438643} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d62ff8d-95ed-5dd5-9434-def79d563c0e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d1129e6-cd92-58d0-8181-e4616216f936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438644} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa956fd-de7f-5971-bd20-88593e558254" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aa956fd-de7f-5971-bd20-88593e558254" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438645} :answer-field/id #uuid "572d6ef2-b778-5091-9ae8-150ff55b2bb6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439351}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90e895ee-1be8-55c1-ab2d-a3596627f1b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-97487" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4x{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-4x{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/96/96c937cf10d45d8870a4a56e257d184dcf2e4caf11312c05df9f385f9c5ee7a8.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}]}
